<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-FRENCH OAKS RESULT FROM CHANTILLY.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-FRENCH OAKS RESULT FROM CHANTILLY.</headline>
<dateline>CHANTILLY, France 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Prix de</p>
<p>Diane-Hermes (French Oaks) for three-year-old fillies run over</p>
<p>1mile 2 1/2f (2.1 kms) on Sunday. 1. Vereva (ridden by Gerald</p>
<p>Mosse) 2. Mousse Glacee (Thierry Thulliez) 3. Brilliance</p>
<p>(Sylvain Guillot) 4. Ryafan (Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>12 ran. Distances: A length and a half, two lengths, half a</p>
<p>length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Aga Khan, trained by Alain de</p>
<p>Royer-Dupre in France.</p>
<p>Value to the winner: $264,000. Pari-Mutuel (including</p>
<p>one-franc stake); Win 3.70 (coupled with Darashandeh); places</p>
<p>1.60, 2.20, 1.40. Dual forecast 26.70</p>
</text>
